xfce4-terminal: embed Hack Braille and make it the default font

Compile Hack Braille (Hack 3.003 plus the braille patterns U+2800..U+28FF,
four styles; MIT and Bitstream Vera License) into xfce4-terminal and
default font-name to "Hack Braille 12".  The fonts are registered with
fontconfig from memory (memfd) at startup; nothing is installed.  A font
set in the preferences still wins.  Adds a fontconfig dependency.

Needs hack-braille-3.003/ (HackBraille-*.ttf, LICENSE.md, README,
mkhackbraille.py) unpacked into the source tree.
Apply after xfce4-terminal-1.2-paste-warning-default-false.patch.

Commits (branch embedded-font on xfce4-terminal-1.1.5):
  5c76cf1 Embed Hack Braille and make it the default font

